course: dictionary
lesson: 11530
title: The almanac: a yearly book of facts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An almanac is a book that is published every year. It has a calendar and facts such as sunrise times, tides, the phases of the moon and weather predictions. «Dad checked the almanac to see when the moon would be full.» The word tells you the book is new each year and full of useful information.
explain: Some almanacs are about one subject. A sports almanac is a yearly book of facts and figures about sport, such as results and records. «The sports almanac listed every winner of the big race.» Look at the words around almanac to see which kind of almanac the writer means.
explain: Almanacs are old. Long ago, farmers used them to plan when to plant their seeds. Today they still list records and facts. Use the context clues first, then check a dictionary if you are not sure.
fact: An almanac is a book published every year.
fact: Almanacs often include a calendar, sunrise times, tides, the moon's phases and weather predictions.
fact: Farmers in the past used almanacs to plan when to plant crops.
fact: Benjamin Franklin wrote a famous almanac called «Poor Richard's Almanack».
fact: A sports almanac is a yearly book of facts and figures about sport.
exercise: «Mum checked the almanac to find out when the moon would be full.» What is an almanac? | A bag for carrying shopping | A kind of small fish | *A book with a yearly calendar and facts about the sky and weather
exercise: «The sports almanac listed every winner of the big race for a hundred years.» What kind of facts would a sports almanac contain? | *Results and records from sport | Songs for the school choir | Recipes for cooking dinner
exercise: «Farmers used the almanac to plan when to plant their seeds.» Copy the word that names the yearly book. | plant | Farmers | *almanac | seeds
test: «Benjamin Franklin wrote Poor Richard's Almanack.» What kind of book was this? | A cookbook for picnics | A novel about pirates | A comic strip | *A yearly book of facts and advice
test: Why would a farmer in the past check an almanac? | To buy a new tractor | *To plan when to plant | To find a lost dog | To learn to swim
exam: Which book would help you find the winners and records of last year's cup? | A cookery book | A bedtime story book | *A sports almanac | A road atlas
